WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.220
Incomplete? A masterpiece? "Across the&nbsp;
Spider-Verse" has seemingly drummed up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.000
every opinion in the multiverse. Here's&nbsp;
what early Twitter reviews have to say.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.920
Of the many Spider-Man-centric projects to release&nbsp;
in the past few years, few have built up as much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.840
hype as "Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse." The&nbsp;
long-awaited sequel to the 2018 hit "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.380
Into the Spider-Verse" has taken a&nbsp;
while to reach the silver screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.060
but it looks to be more than worth the wait.&nbsp;
In continuing the story of Miles Morales,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.380
who has come into his own as his universe's&nbsp;
Spider-Man, the film will showcase a litany&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.526
of Spider-People from all corners of&nbsp;
the seemingly infinite multiverse.

00:00:35.526 --> 00:00:37.308
"You?"
"Wait, you?"

00:00:37.308 --> 00:00:39.358
"You?"

00:00:39.358 --> 00:00:42.480
Unlike his first exposure to the&nbsp;
multiverse, however, this time around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.700
it seems that Miles doesn't solely encounter new&nbsp;
allies. From the villain known as the Spot to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.740
universe-hopping, vampiric Spider-Man of the&nbsp;
year 2099, to countless other Spider-Beings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.980
it appears that Miles has his work cut&nbsp;
out for him as he navigates different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.460
universes. Thankfully, he has old&nbsp;
friends on his side to help him out.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:04.500
As "Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse" begins&nbsp;
its run on the silver screen, the vast majority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.300
of fans have already taken to social media&nbsp;
to sing the film's praises. One user tweeted:

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:14.400
"This is the best Spiderman movie. This is&nbsp;
the best animated movie. This is the best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.480
movie. This is a work of art that flew by and&nbsp;
I want to watch this again a million times."

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:23.280
After calling it their pick for best movie of&nbsp;
the year, another user highlighted the sheer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.488
artistry of the feature by assessing&nbsp;
every single frame as a "masterpiece."

00:01:27.488 --> 00:01:29.329
"I'd pay good money to see that."

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:31.920
Meanwhile, at least one person&nbsp;
admitted that it surpassed their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.580
expectations and even overtook its&nbsp;
predecessor in their eyes. Other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.140
users took to comparing it to other films on&nbsp;
the Marvel and DC slate, with one writing:

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.100
"Across the spiderverse just embarrasses&nbsp;
every other [comic book movie]."

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.580
One common theme among fans is that even&nbsp;
though they just saw it for the first time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:51.300
they're already up for another "Across&nbsp;
the Spider-Verse" screening. And i&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.958
would be wise to prepare for a wild&nbsp;
ending, according to tweet that read:

00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:58.442
"THAT ENDING I NEED TO TALK TO&nbsp;
SOMEONE WHY WOULD YOU DO THAT TO ME."

00:01:58.442 --> 00:02:02.640
Even though "Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse"&nbsp;
is only just now in theaters, those who've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.140
seen it early are already looking toward the&nbsp;
future. "Spider-Man: Beyond the Spider-Verse"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:12.360
has been announced as the film's follow-up, thus&nbsp;
completing the "Spider-Verse" trilogy, and "Across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.980
the Spider-Verse" has fans more than ready to see&nbsp;
what the threequel has in store. One user wrote:

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:20.220
"Across the spiderverse is an absolute masterpiece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.340
and I think it'll only be beaten&nbsp;
by whatever the hell part 2 is."

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.460
Another person, who referred&nbsp;
to "Across the Spider-Verse"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.500
as "peak cinema" in their Twitter post, added:

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.720
"Beyond the spider-verse can't come soon enough."

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.320
Many folks appear to agree, and&nbsp;
that's largely because "Across"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.860
and "Beyond" are the first and second&nbsp;
parts of a whole story. Thus, as one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.760
fan points out, "Across" might feel like&nbsp;
an incomplete story to many moviegoers.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.500
"Spider-Man: Across the Spider-Verse" has been&nbsp;
showered with love and positivity from all sides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:50.280
with the only truly divisive element of it&nbsp;
being whether it deserves to be placed above&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.520
"Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse"&nbsp;
or not. You can now determine where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.360
you stand since the long-awaited sequel is&nbsp;
currently playing exclusively in theaters.

